nter\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/wordpress-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Online WordPress Course<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">FAQs About HTML Syllabus<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block\"><div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784607791706\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">1. Is HTML easy to learn for beginners?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Yes, HTML is one of the easiest skills to start with. It uses simple tags to structure content, so most beginners can grasp the basics within a few days of regular practice.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784607803464\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">2. Is HTML a programming language?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">No, HTML is a markup language, not a programming language.\u00a0It structures and displays content on web pages but does not handle logic or calculations the way languages like JavaScript or <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/python\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Python<\/a> do.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784607816068\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">3. What is the difference between HTML and HTML5?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">HTML is the original markup language, while HTML5 is its latest version. HTML5 adds modern features like audio, video, canvas, and semantic tags that make web pages more interactive and mobile-friendly.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784607829651\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">4. In which order should I follow the HTML syllabus topics?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Start with the basics like elements, tags, and attributes, then move to lists, links, tables, and forms. Finish with advanced topics such as canvas, SVG, and accessibility for a complete foundation.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784607852283\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">5. Which software do I need to start writing HTML?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">You only need\u00a0a simple text\u00a0editor like Notepad or VS Code and any web browser. No paid software is\u00a0required, which makes HTML very beginner-friendly to start with.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784607866799\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">6. Can I learn HTML without\u00a0knowing\u00a0CSS and JavaScript?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Yes, you can learn HTML on its own since it works independently to structure web pages. CSS and JavaScript are added later to handle design and interactivity once your HTML basics are strong.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784607881044\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">7. Can I get a job by learning only HTML?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">HTML alone is a strong starting point but usually not enough for most jobs. Pairing it with CSS and JavaScript opens roles in web development, web design, and front-end development.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784607894943\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">8. Should I learn HTML or Python first?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">If your goal is web development, start with HTML because it builds the structure of every website. Python is better suited for backend, data, and general programming, so it can come later.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784607909084\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">9. Is this HTML course syllabus available for self-study?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Yes, this HTML course syllabus is arranged in a clear order so you can study it on your own. Each topic builds on the\u00a0